---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms &amp; Conditions"
  description="Terms and conditions for Signing Day Advisors services."
  noindex
>

<header class="page-header">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Client Agreement</span>
    <h1>Terms & Conditions</h1>
    <p class="effective">Effective Date: September 25, 2026</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="terms-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="terms-document">

      <p class="terms-intro">These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern the purchase and use of services provided by Signing Day Advisors (“SDA,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). By purchasing an SDA service, the Client agrees to these Terms.</p>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>1. Who the Client Is</h2>
        <p>The “Client” is the adult who purchases or authorizes the SDA service.</p>
        <p>If the student-athlete is under 18, the Client must be the student-athlete’s parent or legal guardian. The minor student-athlete is not a party to this agreement.</p>
        <p>If the student-athlete is 18 or older, the student-athlete may be the Client or another adult may purchase the service for them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>2. Services</h2>
        <p>SDA provides college athletic recruiting guidance, assessments, educational materials, strategic recommendations, and related advisory services. The scope of a service is the scope described for that service at the time of purchase.</p>
        <p>SDA is an independent advisory service and is not an admissions office, college or university, athletic department, scholarship provider, athletic conference, or representative of any school. SDA is not affiliated with or endorsed by the NCAA, the Ivy League, any athletic conference, or any college or university.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>3. No Guarantee of Admission, Recruitment, Scholarship, or Roster Placement</h2>
        <p>SDA provides advisory and educational services only. We do not guarantee admission, recruitment, coach interest or response, scholarship, roster placement, team placement, or any other recruiting, admissions, athletic, academic, or financial outcome.</p>
        <p>Those decisions are made independently by colleges, universities, coaches, athletic departments, admissions offices, and other third parties.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>4. SDA Compass and Other Assessments</h2>
        <p>The SDA Compass and similar assessments are estimates based on information available when the assessment is prepared. Scores, classifications, school-fit assessments, rankings, benchmarks, and recommendations are intended to support recruiting strategy, not predict an outcome.</p>
        <p>Recruiting standards, admissions expectations, coaching staffs, team needs, roster availability, athlete performance, and third-party information may change. Assessments may also be affected by information supplied to SDA that is incomplete, inaccurate, or outdated.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>5. Fees, Billing, Cancellations, and Refunds</h2>
        <p>The price shown for a service at checkout is the price that applies to that purchase. Payment is processed through Stripe or another payment processor selected by SDA. SDA does not directly store complete payment-card information.</p>
        <p>If a Client purchases a recurring monthly service, the Client authorizes recurring monthly charges until the service is cancelled. Cancellation stops future renewals after the effective cancellation date.</p>
        <p>Refund eligibility for one-time services depends on whether SDA has begun performing or delivered the purchased service. SDA may decline a refund for a service that has already been substantially performed or delivered, subject to applicable law.</p>
        <p>Unless required by law or expressly stated otherwise by SDA, cancellation of a recurring service does not create a refund for a billing period that has already begun.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>SDA assessments, reports, scoring methods, formulas, methodologies, graphics, written resources, templates, recommendations, and Compass materials remain the intellectual property of SDA unless otherwise agreed in writing.</p>
        <p>Materials provided to a Client are for that Client’s personal recruiting use only. They may not be reproduced, published, resold, distributed, commercially exploited, reverse engineered, or provided to third parties without SDA’s prior written permission.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>7. Privacy and Communications</h2>
        <p>SDA handles personal information as described in its Privacy Policy. By providing contact information, the Client authorizes SDA to communicate with the Client and, where appropriate, the student-athlete about requested or purchased services.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, SDA will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, punitive, or similar losses arising out of or relating to SDA’s services or any recruiting, admissions, scholarship, athletic, academic, or educational decision or outcome.</p>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, SDA’s total liability for any claim arising out of or relating to these Terms or SDA’s services will not exceed the amount actually paid by the Client for the affected service.</p>
        <p>Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability, rights, or remedies that cannot legally be excluded or limited.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, except to the extent that non-waivable law in the Client’s state of residence provides otherwise.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block arbitration-block">
        <h2>10. Binding Arbitration and Individual Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p><strong>Please read this section carefully. It affects how disputes may be resolved.</strong></p>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, disputes, claims, or controversies arising out of or relating to these Terms, SDA’s services, or the relationship between the Client and SDA will be resolved by final and binding arbitration administered by the American Arbitration Association under the rules applicable to the dispute, rather than by a judge or jury in court.</p>
        <p>Arbitration will proceed on an individual basis. To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, neither party may bring or resolve a covered dispute as a class action, collective action, or representative proceeding.</p>
        <p>This section does not override any non-waivable state or federal law. If the law applicable to a Client imposes additional requirements concerning arbitration, notice, venue, fees, waiver, procedure, or available remedies, those mandatory requirements control.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>11. Changes to Services or Terms</h2>
        <p>SDA may make reasonable changes to its methods, tools, processes, resources, service delivery, or these Terms as the business develops. A material change will not retroactively reduce the core service already purchased without the Client’s agreement.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="terms-block">
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions concerning these Terms, payments, services, cancellations, or account matters may be directed to:</p>
        <p><strong>Signing Day Advisors</strong><br>Email: info@signingdayadvisors.com</p>
      </div>

      <div id="checkout-terms-section" style="display:none">

        <p class="legal-note"><strong>Important:</strong> These Terms include a binding arbitration provision and individual-dispute requirement in Section 10. By selecting “I Agree — Proceed to Payment,” you acknowledge that you have reviewed and accepted these Terms. If the student-athlete is under 18, you also confirm that you are the student-athlete’s parent or legal guardian and are entering into this agreement as the Client.</p>

        <div class="acceptance">
          <h2>Agreement</h2>
          <p>Please indicate whether you accept these Terms & Conditions before continuing.</p>

          <div class="actions">
            <button class="btn-accept" id="agreeButton" type="button">I Agree — Proceed to Payment</button>
            <a class="btn-decline" href="/">I Do Not Agree</a>
          </div>

          <div id="stripePayment" style="display:none;margin-top:28px;text-align:center">
            <a class="btn-accept" id="stripeLink" href="https://buy.stripe.com/7sY28r2DA5ov4e0c91dfG02">Continue to Secure Payment</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div id="reference-terms-section" class="terms-footer-note">
        <p>These Terms & Conditions are provided for reference. Clients purchasing SDA services will be asked to review and accept these Terms as part of the checkout process.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</Base>

<style is:global>
.page-header{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:52px 0 42px}
.page-header .eyebrow{display:block;margin-bottom:12px}
.page-header h1{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.1;margin-bottom:10px}
.effective{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}
.terms-section{padding:52px 0 80px}
.terms-document{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:48px 52px}
.terms-intro{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:30px}
.terms-block{margin-bottom:30px}
.terms-block:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.terms-block h2{font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:8px}
.terms-block p,.terms-block li{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#424A51}
.terms-block p+p{margin-top:8px}
.terms-block ul{margin:8px 0 0 20px}
.terms-block li{margin-bottom:5px}
.arbitration-block{border-left:3px solid var(--navy);padding-left:18px}
.legal-note{margin-top:34px;padding:18px 20px;border:1px solid rgba(15,42,74,.18);background:rgba(15,42,74,.035);font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.65}
.acceptance{margin-top:34px;padding-top:30px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.acceptance h2{font-family:'Fraunces',serif;color:var(--navy);font-size:24px;margin-bottom:8px}
.acceptance p{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:24px}
.actions{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.btn-accept,.btn-decline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;padding:13px 22px;border-radius:2px;font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;transition:all .2s}
.btn-accept{background:var(--gold);color:var(--navy);border:1px solid var(--gold)}
.btn-accept:hover{background:var(--gold-soft);border-color:var(--gold-soft)}
.btn-decline{background:#fff;color:var(--muted);border:1px solid var(--line)}
.btn-decline:hover{border-color:#A8A39A;color:var(--ink)}
.terms-footer-note{margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.terms-footer-note p{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:0}
footer p{font-size:12px}

@media(max-width:760px){
  .terms-document{padding:32px 24px}
  .nav-toggle{display:block}
  .nav-links a{padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08)}
  .actions{flex-direction:column}
  .btn-accept,.btn-decline{width:100%}
}
</style>

<script is:inline>
  var checkoutSection = document.getElementById('checkout-terms-section');
  var referenceSection = document.getElementById('reference-terms-section');

  var params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
  var isCheckoutFlow = params.get('checkout') === '1';

  if (isCheckoutFlow) {
    if (checkoutSection) checkoutSection.style.display = 'block';
    if (referenceSection) referenceSection.style.display = 'none';
  } else {
    if (checkoutSection) checkoutSection.style.display = 'none';
    if (referenceSection) referenceSection.style.display = 'block';
  }

  var agreeButton = document.getElementById('agreeButton');
  var stripePayment = document.getElementById('stripePayment');

  if (agreeButton && stripePayment) {
    agreeButton.addEventListener('click', function () {
      stripePayment.style.display = 'block';
      agreeButton.style.display = 'none';
      stripePayment.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    });
  }
</script>
